% AUTHOR: implementation-absys (an agent: Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5). One text for absys, absys-depth-first and absys-wake-back.
% PRECURSOR-SEEN: no. Not any E01-E09 program (see programs/absys/README.md for what was read).
% NOTATION: 1969 (.ab1), the earliest notation with every construct used (systems/absys/README.md, Notation).
% IDIOM: arithmetic as an assertion in any direction, a = b + 1: Foster and Elcock 1969 (tutorial ch. 8; examples/alternatives.ab1); the three relations as written, u+v = 16, w*u = v, u+10 = 12: Elcock 1982 p. 123 (examples/relation-list.ab2).
% P02b. Unknowns u, v, w (integers). One relation per stage; the harness gives part order[k-1] at stage k (harnesses/absys/README.md, 3.5).
% CONSTANTS BEGIN
r1sum = 16   % part R1
r3add = 10   % part R3
r3sum = 12   % part R3
% CONSTANTS END
% PART R1
u + v = r1sum
% PART R2
w * u = v
% PART R3
u + r3add = r3sum
